    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d638">

                <pb facs="0761" n="675" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg675"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Clayton.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-10-15"><hi rendition="#italic">October 15,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Hay instructs Mr. Clayton to request of the Government of Mexico the
                    provisional arrest and detention of Charles Kratz for bribery in Missouri, where
                    warrant of arrest has been issued.</p>
                <p>Mr. Hay states that formal papers are being prepared; that the Mexican law of
                    1897 will be fully complied with; that strict reciprocity is promised by the
                    Government of the United States; and that the fugitive is said to be at
                    Guadalajara.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
